951,"pass_rate":0.5538,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5789,"def_epa_per_play":0.1845},{"week":8,"opponent":"SEA","home":false,"pf":34.0,"pa":17.0,"off_snaps":69,"epa_per_play":0.1754,"pass_rate":0.5072,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5424,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1627}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"MIN","distance":0.6287,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2022,"team":"DET","distance":0.7057,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.7074,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2022,"team":"LA","distance":0.7416,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean McVay"},{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":0.7523,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"DAL","distance":0.219,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"},{"season":2025,"team":"TB","distance":0.2235,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Todd Bowles"},{"season":2025,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3586,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.4095,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2022,"team":"ARI","distance":0.411,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Bears are 6-2 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 214 to 160. The offense ranks 9th in EPA per play and the defense 12th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the 2nd highest play-action rate and the 3rd most pass rushers in the league.","offense":"The Bears offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest play-action rate in the league. Caleb Williams has run the passing game, with Luther Burden III leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Bears defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been sack rate, where it ranks 2nd, and its weakest has been explosive play rate allowed, where it ranks 24th. Montez Sweat has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Kyler Gordon, who has 4 sacks despite playing only 50% of the snaps. In terms of scheme, they have the 3rd most pass rushers in the league.","special":"The Bears have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 50% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 76% of field goals, which is well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 8% of the money on the books.","players":"Caleb Williams has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,267 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Luther Burden III and Colston Loveland leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. D'Andre Swift has handled most of the work in the backfield with 59% of the carries. On defense, Austin Booker leads the team with 4 sacks.","coaching":"Ben Johnson is calling the offense as head coach and Dennis Allen is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2022 Lions under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Cowboys under Dan Quinn and the 2025 Buccaneers under Todd Bowles.","trends":"The offense went from 8th in EPA per play in 2025 to 9th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 19th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 12th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 12% to 0%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}